From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xucy10 <xucy0609@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 01 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Allay interaction desync on rejected interaction

When two Allays are leashed together and moving, right-clicking an Allay
can cause client inventory/equipment desynchronization. The root cause is
that in handleInteract, the target interaction is guarded by:

  target != null && TickThread.isTickThreadFor(target) && ...

When this condition is false (e.g., the target is on a different tick
thread region), the packet is silently ignored without sending any
corrective inventory/equipment packets. The client may have already
predicted the interaction (consuming an item or updating equipment),
resulting in a visual desync that persists until the player opens/closes
their inventory.

This patch adds a resync path for the rejected interaction case:
1. Resend the player's authoritative inventory/container state.
2. If the target is a LivingEntity (Allay, horse, etc.), schedule an
   equipment resync on the target entity's own region to ensure thread
   safety.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
--- a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
@@ -3044,6 +3044,28 @@
 				}
 			}
 			// Paper start - PlayerUseUnknownEntityEvent
+			// Paper start - Fix Allay interaction desync on rejected interaction
+			else if (target != null) {
+				// The target exists but the interaction was rejected (wrong tick thread or outside world border).
+				// The client may have predicted the interaction and updated its local state, so we must
+				// resend the authoritative player inventory and target equipment to correct any desync.
+				InteractionHand resyncHand = packet.hand();
+				if (io.papermc.paper.util.MCUtil.clientPredictsInteraction(ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.this.player, target, ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.this.player.getItemInHand(resyncHand))) {
+					ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.this.player.containerMenu.sendAllDataToRemote();
+				} else {
+					ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.this.player.containerMenu.forceHeldSlot(resyncHand);
+				}
+				if (target instanceof LivingEntity) {
+					final Entity finalTarget = target;
+					target.getBukkitEntity().taskScheduler.schedule(
+						(Entity p) -> {
+							if (!finalTarget.isRemoved()) {
+								ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.this.send(new net.minecraft.network.protocol.game.ClientboundSetEquipmentPacket(
+									finalTarget.getId(), java.util.Arrays.stream(net.minecraft.world.entity.EquipmentSlot.values())
+									.map((slot) -> com.mojang.datafixers.util.Pair.of(slot, ((LivingEntity) finalTarget).getItemBySlot(slot).copy()))
+									.collect(Collectors.toList()), true));
+							}
+						},
+						null, 0L
+					);
+				}
+			}
+			// Paper end - Fix Allay interaction desync on rejected interaction
 			else if (target == null) {
 				CraftEventFactory.callPlayerUseUnknownEntityEvent(ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.this.player, packet.entityId(), false, packet.hand(), packet.location());
 			}
